        "1.1 The beginner's mistake: building the company before proving the business\nA common beginner mistake is to start with the visible features of a large company: multiple products, several funnels, a team, complex software, paid advertising, and elaborate operations. These things can look like progress, but they do not prove that anyone wants to buy.",
