        "6.1 One audience, one offer, one funnel, one outcome\nThe source's simplicity principle can be turned into an operating rule:\n- **One audience**: a clearly defined buyer group.\n- **One core offer**: the primary product or service.\n- **One funnel**: a simple path from discovery to purchase and delivery.\n- **One outcome**: the main result the offer helps the customer pursue.",
        "This does not mean you can never test alternatives. It means you should avoid running many unrelated experiments simultaneously, because you will not know what is working.",
        "6.2 A simple customer journey\nA beginner-friendly funnel can be:\n1. **Discovery**: a person sees a useful post, recommendation, search result, or direct message.\n2. **Interest**: they recognise the problem and visit a page or ask a question.\n3. **Evaluation**: they understand the offer, deliverables, price, and evidence.\n4. **Purchase**: they pay through a straightforward checkout or agreed payment method.\n5. **Delivery**: they receive the product or service and know how to use it.\n6. **Feedback**: you ask what worked, what was confusing, and what remains unresolved.\n7. **Referral or repeat purchase**: when appropriate, satisfied customers may recommend the solution or buy a related offer.",
