        "7.1 Build assets, not only income\nAn asset is something that can continue creating value after the initial work is complete. In a small online business, useful assets can include:\n- A digital product.\n- A repeatable delivery process.\n- A library of original educational content.\n- A documented workflow.\n- A customer relationship list built with appropriate consent.\n- A strong reputation and credible case studies.\n- A useful tool, template, or calculator.\n- A reliable distribution partnership.",
        "Not every asset produces revenue automatically. Assets need maintenance, distribution, and relevance. But they can reduce the amount of work required to create each additional sale.",
        "7.2 AI is leverage, not the business itself\nThe source argues that AI makes capabilities more accessible to solo operators. The practical lesson is to use AI to accelerate appropriate tasks while keeping human responsibility for decisions and quality.",
        "AI can assist with:\n- Research synthesis.\n- Organising customer interview notes.\n- Drafting outlines and first versions.\n- Generating examples and alternative explanations.\n- Repurposing original content into different formats.\n- Creating checklists and standard operating procedures.\n- Summarising customer feedback.\n- Drafting support responses for human review.\n- Analysing structured business data.",
