        "Worksheet G: Customer feedback log\nFor every early customer, record:\n- What they wanted to achieve.\n- Why they chose the offer.\n- What they found most useful.\n- Where they struggled.\n- What result they achieved or have not yet achieved.\n- What they expected but did not receive.\n- What should change in the product.\n- Whether they have explicitly consented to any public use of their feedback.",
        "Checklist: Ready to launch?\n\n**Audience and problem**\n- [ ] I can describe the target customer clearly.\n- [ ] I have evidence that the problem exists.\n- [ ] I understand what customers currently do to solve it.\n- [ ] I know where I can reach relevant people.\n\n**Offer**\n- [ ] The offer solves one specific problem.\n- [ ] The deliverables are concrete.\n- [ ] The promise is honest and realistic.\n- [ ] The price and terms are clear.\n- [ ] The buyer knows what is not included.\n\n**Delivery**\n- [ ] The product or service has been tested.\n- [ ] Payment and delivery work.\n- [ ] Instructions are understandable.\n- [ ] Support and refund expectations are clear.\n- [ ] Customer information is handled responsibly.\n\n**Distribution**\n- [ ] I have selected one primary platform or channel.\n- [ ] I have useful content related to the audience's problems.\n- [ ] I have a clear next step for interested people.\n- [ ] I am not relying on paid ads to compensate for an unvalidated offer.\n\n**Measurement**\n- [ ] I track sales and costs.\n- [ ] I distinguish revenue from profit.\n- [ ] I collect customer feedback.\n- [ ] I have a weekly review habit.\n- [ ] I know what I will test next.",
